ShareButton (components/ShareButton.tsx)
- Single onClick handler `() => void onShare()` on the button (line 58). `onShare` (lines 31-53): tries `navigator.share`, falls back to `navigator.clipboard.writeText(href)`, then flips `copied` state for 1800ms (visible-label swap 'Share' -> 'Copied'). No motion — only CSS color/border/background transitions via `var(--transition-fast)` on `.button` (CSS lines 16-20). No ref on the button yet; would need a `useRef<HTMLButtonElement>(null)` to hook GSAP.

QuoteShare (components/QuoteShare.tsx)
- Each toolbar pill renders with `onClick={() => void onShareClick(target, i)}` (line 217). `onShareClick` (lines 170-185) either `window.open(target.action.url, ...)` for URL share targets (X / Facebook / Bluesky) or `navigator.clipboard.writeText` for copy/link targets — successful copy sets `copiedIndex=i` and the matching button gets `styles.buttonCopied` (gold flash) for 1200ms with the glyph swapping to the `CheckGlyph`.
- Popover container has an existing CSS keyframe entrance: `.popover { animation: quoteShareIn 140ms ease-out; }` defined in QuoteShare.module.css lines 21-33 — opacity 0->1 + translateY(2px)->0 + scale(0.98)->1. Added in PR #181.
- There is also a separate `.fragmentFlash` keyframe for the amber highlight when arriving via a text-fragment deep-link (CSS lines 100-117) — unrelated to click feedback but worth noting since QuoteShare owns it.
- No button refs today; the only ref on the component is `popoverRef` (the container div). A click-feedback hook needs per-button refs OR an event-target-driven `gsap.fromTo(e.currentTarget, ...)`.

Reference pattern already in the codebase — components/LikeButton.tsx lines 39-55:
```
const buttonRef = useRef<HTMLButtonElement>(null);
useGSAP(() => {}, { scope: buttonRef });
const pulse = () => {
  if (!buttonRef.current) return;
  if (prefersReducedMotion()) return;
  gsap.fromTo(buttonRef.current, { scale: 1 },
    { scale: 1.15, duration: 0.1, yoyo: true, repeat: 1, ease: 'power2.out' });
};
```
`pulse()` is invoked at the very top of the click handler (line 59) — synchronously, before the optimistic state flip and the awaited network call.
